  "raw_text": "PLAN \"12-Week Bodyweight Strength Programme (Beginner)\"\nTYPE workout\nVISIBILITY public\n\nGOALS\n  GOAL primary strength:\n    name \"Build foundational upper/lower body strength with minimal equipment, progression over 12 weeks\"\n\nPHASES\n  PHASE \"Phase 1\" (4 weeks):\n    WEEK 1:\n      DAY Monday training 45m \"Full Body Basics 1\":\n        warmup:\n          walking 5 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          push_up 3x8..12 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          bodyweight_row 3x6..10 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          squat 3x10..15 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          glute_bridge 3x12..20 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          plank 3x20..40 seconds rpe 5 rest 30 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          chest_stretch  length 5 minutes\n    WEEK 2:\n      DAY Tuesday training 45m \"Full Body Basics 2\":\n        warmup:\n          jogging_in_place 5 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          push_up 3x9..12 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          inverted_row (use doorway bar) 3x6..10 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          goblet_squat (bodyweight if no weight) 3x12..18 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          hip_bridge 3x12..20 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          side_plank 3x20..40 seconds each side rpe 5\n        cooldown:\n          hip_flexor_stretch  length 5 minutes\n    WEEK 3:\n      DAY Monday training 45m \"Full Body Basics 3\":\n        warmup:\n          high_knees 2 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          push_up 3x10..12 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          pull_up_progression (assisted or negative on doorway bar) 3x4..8 rpe 7 rest 60 seconds\n          squat 3x12..18 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          glute_bridge march 3x12..20 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          planks 3x30..45 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          shoulder_stretch  length 5 minutes\n    WEEK 4:\n      DAY Thursday training 45m \"Deload & Technique\":\n        warmup:\n          march_in_place 4 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          push_up 3x6..10 rpe 5 rest 60 seconds\n          inverted_row 3x6..8 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          bodyweight_backward_lunge 3x8..12 each leg rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n          prone_hover (superman) 3x12..15 rpe 5 rest 60 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          full_body_stretch 5 minutes\n\n  PHASE \"Phase 2\" (4 weeks):\n    WEEK 5:\n      DAY Monday training 50m \"Progression Push/Pull\":\n        warmup:\n          jumping_jack 3 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          push_up 4x8..12 rpe 6 rest 75 seconds\n          pull_up_progression 4x4..8 rpe 7 rest 75 seconds\n          step_up_with_dive_thrust (use doorway if available) 4x8..12 each leg rpe 6 rest 75 seconds\n          glute_bridge 4x12..20 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          chest_shoulder_stretch 5 minutes\n    WEEK 6:\n      DAY Wednesday training 50m \"Lower Focus\":\n        warmup:\n          leg_m swings 3 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          squat 4x12..18 rpe 7 rest 75 seconds\n          glute_bridge march 4x12..20 rpe 6 rest 75 seconds\n          hip_thrust 3x10..15 rpe 7 rest 75 seconds\n          ab_work_cycle 3x20 reps of chosen core moves\n        cooldown:\n          hip_flexor_stretch 5 minutes\n    WEEK 7:\n      DAY Monday training 50m \"Pull Progressions\":\n        warmup:\n          arm_circles 2 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          pull_up_progression 4x4..8 rpe 7 rest 75 seconds\n          inverted_row 4x6..10 rpe 6 rest 75 seconds\n          pistol_branch_counter (assisted) 3x6..10 per leg\n          plank 3x40..60 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          lat_stretch 5 minutes\n    WEEK 8:\n      DAY Thursday training 50m \"Stability & Volume\":\n        warmup:\n          jog_in_place 3 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          push_up 4x10..15 rpe 6 rest 75 seconds\n          row_variant (bodyweight row) 4x8..12 rpe 6 rest 75 seconds\n          squat 4x12..20 rpe 6 rest 75 seconds\n          glute_bridge 4x15..25 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          full_body_stretch 5 minutes\n\n  PHASE \"Phase 3\" (4 weeks):\n    WEEK 9:\n      DAY Monday training 55m \"Strength Peak Prep\":\n        warmup:\n          dynamic_mobility_routine 5 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          push_up 5x6..10 rpe 7 rest 90 seconds\n          pull_up_progression 5x4..8 rpe 7 rest 90 seconds\n          squat 5x8..12 rpe 7 rest 90 seconds\n          hip_thrust 4x8..12 rpe 7 rest 90 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          mobility_cooldown 5 minutes\n    WEEK 10:\n      DAY Wednesday training 55m \"Push/Pull Intensity\":\n        warmup:\n          jumping_jack 3 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          incline_press (sub if no incline: push_up) 4x8..12 rpe 7 rest 90 seconds\n          bent_over_row (or inverted_row) 4x6..10 rpe 7 rest 90 seconds\n          squat with tempo 4x8..12 rpe 7 rest 90 seconds\n          plank_variation 3x45..60 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          shoulder_stretch 5 minutes\n    WEEK 11:\n      DAY Monday training 60m \"Lower Body Strength\":\n        warmup:\n          leg_mobility 5 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          goblet_squat (use household item as weight) 5x6..10 rpe 7 rest 90 seconds\n          lunge 4x8..12 per leg rpe 7 rest 90 seconds\n          glute_bridge 5x12..20 rpe 7 rest 90 seconds\n          calk_raise (standing or seated) 4x12..20 rpe 6 rest 60 seconds\n        cooldown:\n          quad_stretch 5 minutes\n    WEEK 12:\n      DAY Thursday training 60m \"Deload & Review\":\n        warmup:\n          march_in_place 4 minutes\n        main straight_sets:\n          push_up 3x6..10 rpe 5 rest 90 seconds\n          inverted_row 3x6..10 rpe 6 rest 90 seconds\n          bodyweight_circuit: 3 rounds of 10 reps each of air_squat, glute_bridge, plank 30s\n        cooldown:\n          full_body_stretch 5 minutes\n\nSYNTAX RULES APPLY:\n- Rep ranges use two dots: 3x8..12\n- Sets always first: 3x10\n- RPE after: rpe 7\n- Rest in seconds: rest 60 seconds\n- Exercises use canonical names only from list\n- Cardio modalities used only for warmups/cooldowns: walking, jogging_in_place, high_knees, etc. (Within allowed: running, cycling, swimming, rowing, elliptical, jump_rope, walking, hiking)\n- If a requested exercise not in vocab, substitute closest canonical name\n- Plan remains beginner-friendly, no equipment beyond pushups, doorway pull-up bar, and bodyweight accessories\n- Ensure structure follows PLAN TYPE VISIBILITY GOALS PHASES sections",
